<GuidePage path={path} title="CrewAI vs LangGraph vs AutoGen (2026): Which Agent Framework? | Swarmnest" description="CrewAI, LangGraph and AutoGen compared: approach, languages, license, hosting and status. AutoGen is in maintenance mode; here is what to use instead." faqs={faqs} sources={sources}>
<p class="lead">CrewAI, LangGraph and AutoGen are the three best-known open-source frameworks for multi-agent systems. A lot changed in the past year: LangGraph reached 1.0, and AutoGen moved to maintenance mode. Here is how they compare now, checked Oct 29, 2026.</p>
<div class="notice"><strong>AutoGen Is in Maintenance Mode.</strong> Microsoft says AutoGen gets bug fixes and security patches only. New projects should use <a href="https://github.com/microsoft/agent-framework" rel="noopener">Microsoft Agent Framework</a>, its successor.</div>
<h2 id="short-answer">The Short Answer</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Pick CrewAI</strong> to get a team of role-based agents running quickly in Python, with Flows when you need fixed steps.</li>
<li><strong>Pick LangGraph</strong> for production agents that run for a long time, need saved state, retries and human approval, or need TypeScript.</li>
<li><strong>Skip AutoGen for new work.</strong> Use Microsoft Agent Framework instead, and migrate existing AutoGen code with Microsoft's guide.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="compared">CrewAI vs LangGraph vs AutoGen Compared</h2>
<CmpTable cols={['Approach','Languages','License','Status','Hosted Option','Best For']} rows={main} />
<h2 id="how-they-differ">How They Differ</h2>
<h3>Level of Control</h3>
<p>CrewAI is high level: you give each agent a role, goal and tools, and the crew splits the work. LangGraph is low level: you draw the graph of steps yourself and decide exactly what state moves between them. AutoGen sits between, with agents that solve tasks by messaging each other.</p>
<h3>Production Features</h3>
<p>LangGraph's main draw is durable execution: state is saved at each step, so a run can pause for human review or survive a restart and pick up where it stopped. CrewAI Flows add deterministic, event-driven steps and state, and CrewAI AMP adds tracing and deployment.</p>
<h3>Where AutoGen Went</h3>
<p>In October 2025 Microsoft merged AutoGen and Semantic Kernel into Microsoft Agent Framework. Its single-agent interface is close to AutoGen's, and multi-agent work moves to a graph-based workflow API.</p>
<h2 id="others">Other Frameworks Worth a Look</h2>
<CmpTable cols={['What It Is','Pick It If']} rows={others} />
<p>See all of them in the <a href="/directory/agent-frameworks/">Agent Frameworks directory</a>. To give an agent memory, see <a href="/guides/mem0-vs-zep-vs-letta/">Mem0 vs Zep vs Letta</a>; for tools, see <a href="/guides/best-mcp-servers-for-claude-code-and-cursor/">Best MCP Servers for Claude Code and Cursor</a>.</p>
</GuidePage>
